# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tool output. Everything here is regenerated by Vivado/xsim on the next run.
# Expanded 2 Sep -- the old list let ~30 files of clutter accumulate in the
# root (rolling .backup logs, .wdb waveform dumps, whole build directories).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Vivado / xsim journals, logs, rolling backups
*.log
*.jou
*.str
*.pb
*_*.backup.log
*_*.backup.jou
dfx_runtime.txt

# Waveform databases -- regenerate by re-simulating
*.wdb

# Tool scratch
.Xil/
xsim.dir/
.cache/

# Build and project output directories
build/
vivado_proj/
vivado_sim/
vivado_engine/
vivado_engine_kc705/
sim_scripts/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated IP. Commit the .xci RECIPE only (a few kB); ignore everything
# generated from it (tens of MB).
#
# FIXED 3 Sep: the previous list missed `*.gen/`, which is where Vivado puts
# the bulk -- the .dcp checkpoint, 2.8 MB of C-model zips, and the full
# simulation netlists. The first push attempt was 70.17 MiB and aborted
# mid-transfer because of it.
#
# Dropping the generated output costs nothing: check_elab.tcl,
# build_synth.tcl and run_pipeline_smoke.tcl all call read_ip +
# generate_target, so a fresh clone regenerates it on first run.
# Full regeneration from scratch, if ever needed:
#   vivado -mode batch -source scripts/create_fft_ip.tcl   (xfft_0)
#   vivado -mode batch -source build_mig.tcl               (MIG DDR3)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
vivado_ip/
vivado_ip_kc705/*.gen/
vivado_ip_kc705/*.cache/
vivado_ip_kc705/*.hw/
vivado_ip_kc705/*.runs/
vivado_ip_kc705/*.sim/
vivado_ip_kc705/*.ip_user_files/

# MIG / corner-turn test project output
ctm_test/*.gen/
ctm_test/*.cache/
ctm_test/*.hw/
ctm_test/*.runs/
ctm_test/*.sim/
ctm_test/*.ip_user_files/

# Large binaries not referenced by any test
attic/golden_cube.npy

# Reports are regenerated by build_synth.tcl
reports/
